id: pm-zeifd2
title: "Review and audit passes are identified by date and theme, never by sequential numbers"
description: "Standing governance convention: every review, audit, organization, or planning pass recorded in the tracker is named by ISO date plus a descriptive theme. Sequential pass numbering (for example 'audit pass #99' or 'review #17') is prohibited in item titles, bodies, comments, notes, learnings, docs, and linked evidence."
type: Decision
status: open
priority: 1
tags[6]: audit,convention,governance,merge-safety,multi-agent,review
created_at: "2026-07-25T22:08:46.174Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T05:49:27.069Z"
author: "harness:opencode"
estimated_minutes: 30
acceptance_criteria: Convention is recorded on the living roadmap pm-doxj; every future pass is identified by ISO date and descriptive theme; no new sequential pass numbers appear in any tracker surface or doc; historical numbered references remain unaltered as immutable record; enforcement rides the existing tracker data-quality ratchet pm-kpftft
goal: project management = context management
objective: "Keep pass identifiers self-describing, sortable, and safe under thousands of concurrent agents and multi-branch merges"
value: "Date+theme identifiers carry their own context, cannot collide across branches or harnesses, and need no global counter coordination"
why_now: An explicit maintainer directive prohibits numbered audit runs; the tracker already mixes both styles (numbered review #12/#13/#15/#16 and pass 91 versus unnumbered date+theme passes since 2026-07-25) with no recorded governing decision
parent: pm-33cw
risk: low
confidence: high
